# Convergence: technical acceptance

AC-01..04 APPROVED within the governance contract. Eight new fixture tests exercise legal states, legacy aliases, stale/missing/unrelated evidence, document-only promotion, criterion binding and path boundaries. All 42 governance tests pass. Five methods pass in an independent export without application sources. Thirteen existing Rust tests and two focused consumer tests pass.

The nine skills now have 26 APPROVED, 3 INCONCLUSIVE and 25 UNVERIFIED criteria. Eight technical approvals concern frozen evaluated consumers only. Existing historical agent trial reviews remain limited to their actual responses; no new agent evaluation is claimed. The original 36 scenario contracts and historical envelopes are unchanged.

The validator checks explicit evidence bindings, not authenticity, semantic sufficiency or execution authority. Inconclusive UI focus/heartbeat and plugin persistence observations are not promoted. Missing index, graph, ledger, output, sandbox, publication integration and concurrent-workspace capabilities remain unverified. Details: docs/validation/technical-acceptance-20261101/review.md.
